# What every OpenSigner image needs to come up and be used, whatever it
# runs on. A driver that quietly loses a dependency — because the
# subsystem above it went out — fails here rather than on the owner's desk.

BLK_DEV_INITRD       the whole root filesystem is linked into the kernel image
DEVTMPFS_MOUNT       the kernel makes /dev itself; nothing in the image could
FB                   the interface the shell writes every frame through
VT                   the framebuffer console owns the display until the app's first frame, and it needs a virtual terminal
FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE  what paints the boot logo, so a black display means the firmware and not a silent working device
INPUT_EVDEV          /dev/input/eventN, which is how the shell reads touches, keys and pointers
VIDEO_DEV            /dev/video0, the V4L2 node the scanner opens
USB_VIDEO_CLASS      a USB webcam is a camera every one of these devices supports
VFAT_FS              the exchange partition, where a PSBT arrives and a signed one goes back
